{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-152729-r4675785","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Nasi Goreng (Indonesian Fried Rice)","sourcePageId":152729,"sourceRevision":"4675785","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-10-13T05:46:44Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Arlorecruitz","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Nasi%20Goreng%20(Indonesian%20Fried%20Rice)&oldid=4675785","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:24.376Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indonesian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bitter bean","Category:Recipes using chicken","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using coconut oil","Category:Recipes using corned beef","Category:Recipes using cucumber","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using hot dog","Category:Recipes using liver","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes with metric units"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"4d3ad61d1be99b05bae869401b696dce2f6dc7c8ea4284a9ae0e4b20fff04a1e","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Indonesian recipes|servings=2|time=20 minutes|difficulty=2\n}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Indonesia|Cuisine of Indonesia]]\n== Ingredients ==\n*2 servings of [[Cookbook:Steamed Rice|steamed rice]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n*1 clove [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Shallot|shallots]]\n*1 red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile pepper]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Fish Oil|fish oil]]\n*10 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Coconut oil|coconut oil]]\n*Sweet [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n*Salty soy sauce or [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*Ground pepper\n\n=== Optional ingredients ===\n*20 [[Cookbook:Bitter Bean|stink beans]] or [[Cookbook:Green Bean|green beans]]\n*100 g [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] fillet, cut into small pieces\n*100 g small [[Cookbook:Prawn|prawns]]\n*4 fish meatballs\n*2 spoons of tinned [[Cookbook:Corned Beef|corned beef]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cucumber|cucumber]]\n*[[Cookbook:Slicing|Sliced]] [[Cookbook:Hot Dog|hot dogs]] or [[Cookbook:Sausage|sausages]]\n*Sliced [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] [[Cookbook:Liver|liver]]\n*[[Cookbook:Cauliflower|Cauliflower]]\n*Sliced salted dried fish\n*[[Cookbook:Green Onion|Spring onion]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Slice shallots and red pepper into thin slices.\n# Crush garlic, peel of the skin, and [[Cookbook:Mince|mince]] well.\n# Slice stinky beans in half, or as desired.\n# Heat oil in [[Cookbook:Wok|wok]], add the chicken or prawn, and [[Cookbook:Stir-frying|stir fry]] until done.\n# Add shallot, pepper, garlic and stink beans. Stir until garlic turns golden.\n# Crack in the eggs, and stir fry until half done.\n# Add the steamed rice, and stir until all mixed.\n# Add soy sauces, salt, and ground pepper as desired.\n# Serve on plates, adding fresh cucumber slices or tomatoes as garnish.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n*Use cold rice, preferably leftover from a day before. Unsticky rice is easier to cook and preferred by some.\n*Some prefer not to use stinky beans and use green peas or green beans as a substitute. This will give a nice shade of green.\n\n=== Variations ===\n*If you are cooking with corned beef, leave the sweet soy sauce out. This is a variation of nasi goreng called ''nasi goreng kornet'' or corned beef fried rice.\n*Try including a sunny side up egg as accompaniment on the side.\n*Some also prefer adding vegetables such as cucumber and tomatoes.\n*You can use salted fish as a variation to make ''nasi goreng ikan asin'', or salted fish fried rice. In this case, leave out the sweet soy sauce.\n*Substitute green peas with sliced spring onions, adding them after the rice has been added to the wok. Spring onions will give nice aroma and color to the fried rice.\n*Prawn cracker/chips are a nice condiment on the side.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Indonesian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corned beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bitter bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hot dog]]\n[[Category:Recipes using liver]]\n\n[[ta:சமையல் நூல்/மரக்கறி நாசி கொரெங்]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Nasi Goreng (Indonesian Fried Rice)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 servings of steamed rice","sourceText":"2 servings of steamed rice","amountText":"2 servings of steamed rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 eggs","sourceText":"2 eggs","amountText":"2 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 clove garlic","sourceText":"1 clove garlic","amountText":"1 clove garlic","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 shallots","sourceText":"2 shallots","amountText":"2 shallots","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 red chile pepper","sourceText":"1 red chile pepper","amountText":"1 red chile pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-